{
  "about": "Time words and counts in a message, one rule for Express and the agent service (docs/02 §2.11.1 rule 5, docs/04 §4.7). Express reads it in server/test/period.test.js (T41, TC-F14-25); the agent service's pytest reads the same file when period.py is built (T45). Each row gives a message `text`, the phrases `found` in it, in the order they are typed, each with its `kind` and its words exactly as typed, and `rest`, the words that no phrase took, joined by one space. A phrase's numbers are never an amount. Matching rules: the text is split on whitespace after a leading '+'; a word is compared in lower case without accents and without punctuation around it, so 'Ngày?' reads as 'ngay' (the one exception: 'ngày' needs its accent, see 'days'); a number is only digits, and a number followed by a money unit written apart ('k', 'nghìn', 'tr', 'triệu', 'm', 'ng', 'ngàn', 'đ', 'vnd') or joined to it ('10k') is money, never part of a phrase. Kinds: 'day' = hôm nay, hôm qua, hqua, yesterday; 'week' = tuần này, tuần trước, cuối tuần; 'month' = tháng này, tháng trước, tháng N (N 1-12, two digits at most), also with 'năm YYYY' after it (YYYY 1900-2099); 'year' = năm YYYY (1900-2099) and tháng YYYY (2000-2099); 'date' = dd/mm and dd/mm/yyyy (day 1-31, month 1-12; it only has to look like a date, 31/02 is not checked here); 'days' = N ngày (N 1-366) when 'ngày' is written with its accent (in NFC or NFD form) or when qua, trước or nay follows it, the word that follows belongs to the phrase; 'items' = N khoản (N 1-50); 'top' = top N (N 1-999) only when 'top' is the first word. Not here yet: date ranges. period.py adds what each phrase means against `today` (docs/07 §7.9.2 'period rules'), and this file gets that part then.",
